    <md:content-id>m02331</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.1.0: Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>601dd281-dc72-42a9-b178-56e2b133769f</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you will gain understanding of the structure of perfect-square expressions. This lesson will also help you see that perfect squares can be handy for solving equations because we can find their square roots.</para>
<para>When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list>
  <item> Recognize perfect-square expressions written in different forms.</item>
  <item> Recognize quadratic equations that have a perfect-square expression and solve the equations.</item>
</list>
<para>Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list>
  <item> 9.1.1: Equations with Quadratic Expressions on Both Sides of the Equal Sign</item>
  <item> 9.1.2: Recognizing Structure in Perfect-Square Expressions</item>
  <list>
    <item> 9.1.2: Self Check</item>
    <item> 9.1.2: Additional Resources</item>
  </list>
  <item> 9.1.3: Solving Multi Step Quadratic Equations Using Perfect Squares</item>
  <list>
    <item> 9.1.3: Self Check</item>
    <item> 9.1.3: Additional Resources</item>
  </list>
  <item> 9.1.4: Explain Why an Expression Is a Perfect Square</item>
</list>
<para>After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list>
  <item> 9.1.5: Practice</item>
  <item> 9.1.6: Lesson Summary</item>
</list></section>
</content>
</document>
